The function checks whether a list of at least three points, given in order as vertices of a simple polygon, forms a convex shape. A polygon is non-convex if any immediate interior angle is greater than 180 degree, and a sequence of collinear points is never convex.

The test runs across all three-point segments of the polygon, repeating the loop back to the start once for the pair that crosses the gap between the last and first point. It measures the orientation of each segment with the signed area formula (which here is twice the area of the triangle and also twice the determinants from previous symmetries), alternating with the preceeding direction:

